                                "sense_id": "8e2cdf04-fbc5-308c-be76-59fd4d9964c4",
                                "text": "In Mauritanian Hassaniya, forms like lil-i can function nominally ('mine'), and accordingly have FeSg and Pl variants (lil-t-i, lwaayl-i), see DHF l.lxxv."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52d59285-993d-48dd-9128-c8f5e4ce05f5",
                                "sense_id": "8e2cdf04-fbc5-308c-be76-59fd4d9964c4",
                                "text": "In the first phase, the grasp of an abstraction, the concept 'size' does not function nominally, rather it provides a way of thinking the quality of something."
